AUTO CODE REVIEW TASK

Workspace: {{workspace}}
Diff command: {{diff_command}}
Review focus: {{review_focus}}
Severity floor: {{severity_floor}}
Pipeline step: {{pipeline_step}}
Previous results: {{previous_results}}

Run the diff command from the workspace, inspect the changed files needed to validate findings, and perform a high-signal review. Do not modify files. Do not run destructive git commands. Treat spec/, intent/, and formal/ as authoritative when touched by the diff.

Write a RESULT file at the workspace root containing valid JSON with this shape:
{
  "signal": "pass|fix|fail",
  "summary": "one concise sentence",
  "verdict": "PASS|FIX|FAIL",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "BLOCKER|CRITICAL|MAJOR|MINOR",
      "path": "relative/file",
      "line": 1,
      "problem": "one sentence",
      "why_it_matters": "one sentence",
      "suggested_fix": "specific action"
    }
  ],
  "stats": {"files": 0, "insertions": 0, "deletions": 0},
  "evidence": []
}

Use FAIL for any BLOCKER or CRITICAL issue, FIX for MAJOR-only issues, and PASS when there are no blocker or major findings. If there are no findings, findings must be an empty array.
